  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>MoSPI, "Women and Men in India": a multi-source compendium. Each indicator draws on its own underlying source: the Census of India (sex ratio 1951-2011, literacy to 2011), the Sample Registration System (fertility, IMR, life expectancy, MMR), NFHS (health behaviours), PLFS (labour force, 2017-18 onward), and NCRB (crime). Retrieved via the eSankhyiki API, vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>. The 17 core indicators forming this guide's spine are ingested in full; the remaining ~140 catalogued indicators (time use, banking schemes, political representation, disability, cyber crime) live in the raw audit dump.</p>
        <p>No indicator is spliced or chained with another. The varying cadences, census decadal, SRS annual, MMR three-year moving periods, life-expectancy five-year cohorts, make a shared date axis impossible and a forced one dishonest. Each plate carries its own axis and its own source citation. Values marked '-' at source are null; years marked '*' are projections.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>The sex ratio is a 2011 stock count: no census has been held since. Life expectancy periods after 2016-20 are projections (marked '*', dashed on the chart). The sharp rise in female LFPR after 2017-18 is partly a measurement-frame effect (PLFS coverage and recall widened); Guide 06 carries the fuller labour-force detail. Every indicator is final as its underlying source publishes; the compendium is curated, not revised.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Social, version 1.0, covers the gender panorama: sex ratio (the 70-year census story), survival (IMR crossover, MMR decline, life-expectancy convergence), fertility (TFR by education), education (the literacy gap), work (the LFPR gap) and state dispersion. Next scheduled revision: on release of the next compendium update or the 2025 Census.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fine">
      <span>India Atlas, Women and Men in India</span>
      <span>Vintage <span id="prov-vintage2">–</span>, multi-source, never spliced</span>
      <span>Set in Source Serif 4 and Golos Text</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

